yourdomain.com

# ── How to use a custom domain ──────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Rename this file to exactly  CNAME  (no extension) and put your
#    apex or subdomain on the first line, nothing else.
# 2. At your DNS provider add either:
#      • Apex domain (yourdomain.com) → four A records pointing to
#        185.199.108.153, 185.199.109.153, 185.199.110.153, 185.199.111.153
#      • Subdomain (www.yourdomain.com) → CNAME to yourhandle.github.io
# 3. Repo → Settings → Pages → Custom domain → enter the same domain,
#    then tick "Enforce HTTPS" once the certificate is issued.
# 4. Update the domain in index.html (canonical + Open Graph),
#    robots.txt and sitemap.xml.
#
# Delete these comment lines from the real CNAME file — GitHub expects
# the domain alone.
